    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XALTqTWCb7mgCXkNn1TRLx)_\n\n## What\n\nNew option `sp-thesis-dump-trust-local-variables` (default `nil`). When on, `enable-local-variables` is bound to `:all` only in the two places where the module triggers local-variable processing: reading the project's `.dir-locals.el` (`sp-thesis-dump--local-values`) and visiting the task file (`sp-thesis-dump-commit`). Nothing global changes.\n\n## Risk\n\nEvery variable in those files is applied without a question, including ones that can run code (hooks, `eval` forms where `enable-local-eval` allows). The docstring and the `Trusting local variables` section of the doc say so. The option has no `:safe` predicate, so a `.dir-locals.el` cannot turn it on for itself.\n\n## Tested\n\nNo Emacs in the container: checked paren balance, and that the blocks of `sp-thesis-dump.org` agree with `sp-thesis-dump.el` (whitespace-insensitive). Not run in Emacs.\n\nThe branch is named `200-…` because I guessed the number before the PR existed; the PR is #201 and I could not rename the branch from here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCPjeGYLGwpABH9DYo)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCPjeGYLGwpABH9DYo\n",
